# ApiPlatform callback relationship code tour

Initially, I treated `src/GraphQl/Type/FieldsBuilder.php` as the point where GraphQL field callbacks converge. At this point in the reading, I started by inferring relationships from the imports at the top of the file: type definitions, resolver factories, and filters all appeared around the same file, so field construction was presumably wiring these objects together.

```php
use ApiPlatform\GraphQl\Exception\InvalidTypeException;
use ApiPlatform\GraphQl\Resolver\Factory\ResolverFactoryInterface;
use ApiPlatform\GraphQl\Type\Definition\TypeInterface;
use ApiPlatform\Metadata\FilterInterface;
```

The reading at the time was: `TypeInterface` sets field types, `FilterInterface` attaches filter criteria to fields, and `ResolverFactoryInterface` is the source of the callbacks. On that reading, there was no need to trace callback relationships separately from each field definition; coming back to this file first would be enough.

One part doesn't quite fit: `InvalidTypeException` is also imported. It may only handle type mismatches, or it may indicate that field construction stops before callback creation. I haven't yet matched this up with the actual throw site.

The next pass should record where `ResolverFactoryInterface` is used and cross-check against the notes on adjacent calls in DOC-08.

# ApiPlatform legacy code notes

Start with these four direct dependencies from the header of `src/JsonApi/Serializer/ItemNormalizer.php`. The repository index marks it as a baseline source entry point; the names retained here are ItemNormalizer's own immediate neighbors:

```php
use ApiPlatform\Metadata\ApiProperty;
use ApiPlatform\Metadata\Exception\ItemNotFoundException;
use ApiPlatform\Metadata\IriConverterInterface;
use ApiPlatform\Metadata\Property\Factory\PropertyMetadataFactoryInterface;
```

`ApiProperty` and `PropertyMetadataFactoryInterface` are both on the property metadata side: one is a metadata type name, the other a factory interface name. `IriConverterInterface` points to the conversion entry point for resource IRI. `ItemNotFoundException` is the only dependency in the file header under the `Exception` namespace, keeping resource-not-found failures among this file's searchable dependency links.

This note covers only file declarations and dependencies; method names, parameter flow, and surrounding calls are not included. If specific handling branches are found in the file later, add the branch names and corresponding failure samples next to these four names.
